val8=A tetrahedron is a polyhedron in the space with 4 vertices.
val9=If one takes 4 adjacent vertices of a parallelepiped, the tetrahedron	  generated by these 4 vertices has a volume which is 1/6 that of the	  parallelepiped.
val10=The volume of the parallelepiped can be computed via the cross product of vectors.
